[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3924559727","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116462#issuecomment-3924559727","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116462","id":3924559727,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7p7Adv","user":{"login":"komunre","id":49118681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTE4Njgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49118681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre","html_url":"https://github.com/komunre","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T04:00:03Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T04:00:03Z","body":"I'd be glad to make a pull request to fix this issue myself, however I am not familiar with Godot's codebase and therefore unsure where exactly to look for the issue other than \"somewhere in jolt-related code\". I'll keep looking, but it'll take a while.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3924559727/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3927757506","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116462#issuecomment-3927757506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116462","id":3927757506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qHNLC","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T14:47:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T14:47:47Z","body":"It's because your `grab_point` is a `StaticBody3D`. Static bodies are assumed to be static (as in not moved) so have no velocities associated with them, which leads to a bunch of weird issues when you try to move them around like this.\n\nYou'll see weird issues when trying to move static bodies around with Godot Physics as well, but not this exact one.\n\nIf you change `grab_point` to instead be a kinematic body, meaning either an `AnimatableBody3D`, `CharacterBody3D` or a `RigidBody3D` set to `frozen` with `FREEZE_MODE_KINEMATIC`, you should find that it works as expected.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3927757506/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928076617","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116462#issuecomment-3928076617","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116462","id":3928076617,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qIbFJ","user":{"login":"komunre","id":49118681,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTE4Njgx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49118681?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre","html_url":"https://github.com/komunre","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/komunre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T15:40:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T15:40:23Z","body":"Whoops. I think that + inherent flaw with Joint approach that I didn't fully grasp back when I worked with it in non-Godot project - that it tends to break down when target position is inside another shape were the reasons for unexpected behavior.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3928076617/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]